Steps to create .bif and .sim formatted vectors from the BusTalk
code (default)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
make <testname>

This will create infile.bif and bif.sim in the ./invec directory

Please refer to the 'makefile' for legal 'testname's.

RUNNING THE COMPLETE TEST SUITE
===============================
All the tests for the Smc cannot be run together because of the 
large bif/tif files that will be created because of the large number of test
cases presnt. Instead the tests have been partitioned into 4 sub-tests to 
facilitate running the complete tests.
They are :
1. Smc1
2. Smc2
3. Smc3
4. Smc4

Please compile these tests seperately, and issue make rtl from the top level 
each time to run the tests. For example, the following string of commands will
compile and run all the tests. After setting all the environment variables 
metioned in the smc_pl092/README file :
From smc_pl092 directory:

cd verification/bustest
make Smc1
cd ../..
make rtl
cd verification/bustest
make Smc2
cd ../..
make rtl
cd verification/bustest
make Smc3
cd ../..
make rtl
cd verification/bustest
make Smc4
cd ../..
make rtl

The above string of commands, can be cut and paste into a file, and sourced
from top level to acheive the same.

